-names></name></person-group><article-title>An MCM2-related gene is expressed in proliferating cells of intact and regenerating planarians.</article-title><source>Dev Dyn</source><year>2000</year><volume>218</volume><fpage>603</fpage><lpage>614</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10906779</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/1097-0177(2000)9999:9999&#x0003c;::AID-DVDY1016&#x0003e;3.0.CO;2-C</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Orii</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Sakurai</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Watanabe</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Distribution of the stem cells (neoblasts) in the planarian <italic>Dugesia japonica</italic>.</article-title><source>Dev Genes Evol</source><year>2005</year><volume>215</volume><fpage>143</fpage><lpage>157</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15657737</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s00427-004-0460-y</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Newmark</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><name><surname>Sanchez Alvarado</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Bromodeoxyuridine specifically labels the regenerative stem cells of planarians.</article-title><source>Dev Biol</source><year>2000</year><volume>220</volume><fpage>142</fpage><lpage>153</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10753506</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1006/dbio.2000.9645</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Benfey</surname><given-names>PN</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Stem cells: a tale of two kingdoms.</article-title><source>Curr Biol</source><year>1999</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>R171</fpage><lpage>172</lpage><pub-id pub-id-typ